        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-88458",
        ":question/problem": "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{x+2}-7x\\cdot {3}^{x+2}+12\\cdot {3}^{x+2}=0?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{x+2}-7x\\cdot {3}^{x+2}+12\\cdot {3}^{x+2} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-7x+12){3}^{x+2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-7x+12=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{3}^{x+2}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-7x+12=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x-3)(x-4)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=3,4.$\n\n- The equation ${3}^{x+2}=0$ has no solutions because ${3}^{x+2}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=3,4,$ and their product is $3\\cdot 4=12.$"
      },
